+# CLEANUP_PARTIALLY_VERIFIED
+
+Delivery: **INSTALLATION_PACKAGE_READY**. Repository: `Morfindien/Bubbleverse`. BASE_SHA: `f689c9ca4a4917909104ea34b0428f46059e4c07`. No remote changes or result commit claimed.
+
+Seven explicitly superseded workflow definitions have been physically moved into browsable archive bundles. Completed failure runs are completion evidence, not scientific success. Their original Git bytes, permissions and historical access were verified. Source programs, scientific statuses, tests, inputs, outputs and all journals retain their original locations and bytes. The canonical registry gains archive-navigation fields only.
+
+All4,827 tracked files were read and hashed. All756Python sources parse; all workflow YAML parses. There are3,805 indexed workflow run blocks and672Python main-guard entries with explicit non-invented-command exclusions. README now leads to root START_CODES.md, structure, journal/prompt navigation and this maintenance history. Existing README content remains verbatim below the new technical header. Root file count is4582→4583; ordinary root moves0, archived workflow bundles7, archived source programs0, deleted files0. Navigation links are separate from moves.
+
+## Verification
+
+Scoped integrity checks pass; one pre-existing missing ACTIVE workflow is BLOCKED (Q039-IMPLBLOCK-V1). Verified coverage includes every nonmutable baseline payload hash/mode, archived original-source retrieval, placement coverage, JSON schema, command IDs, absence of new missing ACTIVE workflow paths and the actual permanent launcher's accept/reject resolver. No remote dispatch, scientific test or numerical campaign ran. There was no numerical algorithm change requiring a new scientific result. Verification is a same-agent pass using original resolver code, not independent scientific replication.
+
+## Limits and deferred work
+
+Every protected/ambiguous original stays in place. Some retired definitions have source/test consumers and are deferred in the placement manifest. Retirement of whole source/config/test bundles needs complete consumer/lifecycle evidence. Historical Markdown/notebook commands have not been exhaustively normalized into the launch registry. External direct-dispatch consumers remain unobserved; supported canonical launchers already reject the archived non-ACTIVE IDs. Existing case-folding collisions remain unchanged and are recorded. Some untracked artifacts appeared during checkout; they were preserved, excluded from the package and never treated as disposable.
+
+The existing maintenance engine is retained unchanged: its preview mode mutates local files, it does not check queued/running jobs, and generated bare program commands can omit required arguments. It was inspected, not run. Do not use its apply workflow to install this exact release; apply the supplied base-bound patch instead.
+
+## Evidence and confidence
+
+OBSERVED: exact tracked bytes, parser results, registry values, completed-run metadata, no queued/in-progress runs at retrieval, local moves and resolver checks. INFERRED: scoped retirement of these workflow definitions from explicit replacement and completion records. UNKNOWN: arbitrary external consumers and all historical launch contexts. No quantitative confidence score or scientific conclusion is added. Repository-wide technical inspection has TARGET_Q=UNSET and does not synthesize later scientific findings. Supplied Q052V67 remains unmodified; no Q-point charge is made for repository maintenance.
+
+## Upgrade coverage
+
+| Supplied upgrade range | Coverage | Evidence / reason |
+|---|---|---|
+|1–23|PRESERVED_EXISTING / VERIFIED|Existing registry and permanent launcher reused; exact-base intake and immutable history checks.|
+|37–46|VERIFIED|Scoped retrieval, no scientific reruns, completion cache/source IDs preserved.|
+|51–70|IMPLEMENTED / DEFERRED_SEPARATE_SCOPE|Seven navigable archives, indexes and inventory schema; whole-bundle migration deferred.|
+|92–101|VERIFIED / DEFERRED_SEPARATE_SCOPE|Local rollback and no dispatch; full external-discovery proof remains unavailable.|
+|106–140|PRESERVED_EXISTING / VERIFIED|Byte/mode/path integrity, UTC hashes and explicit capability/trajectory limits.|
+|146–150|IMPLEMENTED|Retrievable run evidence, bounded checks and precise next action.|
+|24–36,47–50,103–105,142–145|NOT_APPLICABLE|Scientific work outside cleanup authority.|
+|71–91|NOT_APPLICABLE|No publishing, website or analytics task.|
+
+These range labels are scoped coverage, not claims that every upgrade item was implemented. The full150-item source list was not supplied; item-by-item verification is unavailable.
+
+## Next action
+
+Read INSTALL.md, use a clean checkout at the exact base, check the patch, then apply locally. Remote publication/merge remains a separate authorized action. No generic cleanup rerun is needed. The next broader organization task requires consumer closure for specifically deferred bundles, not a repeat of this full byte inventory.
